    <string name="troubleshoot_title">Display troubleshooting</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_intro">Scrambled, partial, or stuck images usually mean the NFC transfer was interrupted or the panel refresh did not finish. Pick what you see, review the last sync, then run a recovery pattern.</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_section">What does the panel look like?</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_hint">Choose a symptom</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_last_sync_section">Last sync attempt</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_recovery_section">Recovery patterns</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_recovery_summary">Each pattern fills the whole panel. If the result is also scrambled, the issue is likely physical (coil contact or module state) rather than your image.</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_physical_section">Physical checklist</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_physical_checklist">• Remove thick phone cases\n• Align the phone\'s NFC coil (upper-back on Samsung) over the module coil\n• Disable Battery Saver; keep screen on\n• Hold flat and still until the app shows Done (~6s typical)\n• Wait 90s between attempts if the module was mid-refresh\n• After a bad transfer, run Clear panel (white) before syncing your image again</string>
