    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_partial_title">Partial overlay</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_partial_cause">Likely cause: NFC dropped mid-upload (phone lifted too early, poor coil contact, or module busy from a prior refresh). Some pixels updated, others did not.</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_partial_fix">Fix: Run Clear panel (white), wait 90 seconds, then sync again. Hold the phone still until Done — do not lift at ~6s unless the app says so.</string>

    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_half_title">Half-updated panel</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_half_cause">Likely cause: refresh phase lost power partway through the physical repaint. Common with weak NFC coupling or moving the phone during the 99% refresh phase.</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_half_fix">Fix: Send the checkerboard test. A clean checkerboard confirms the full panel can refresh. If only one half updates, improve coil alignment and retry.</string>

    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_unchanged_title">No visible change</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_unchanged_cause">Likely cause: module acknowledged the transfer but did not repaint (marginal power), or you synced the same-looking image. Check the last sync progress — if it reached 100% quickly, coupling may be too weak for the repaint.</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_unchanged_fix">Fix: Run the full black test — any real refresh should flash the panel. If black also fails to appear, retry with no case, Battery Saver off, and firm centered contact.</string>

    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_ghost_title">Ghost image</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_ghost_cause">Likely cause: incomplete refresh left prior ink state on the e-paper. E-ink can retain a faint previous image until a full-frame update completes.</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_ghost_fix">Fix: Clear panel (white) twice with 90s between attempts, then sync your image. Avoid re-syncing within the 90s cooldown after success.</string>

    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_inverted_title">Inverted tones</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_inverted_cause">Likely cause: editor Invert was enabled, or a re-dither pass altered the halftone. Less often, a partial transfer can look like inverted regions.</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_inverted_fix">Fix: Re-open the image in the editor and check Invert. Run checkerboard — if the pattern is also wrong, export the diagnostic report and note the last sync driver.</string>

    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_bands_title">Horizontal bands</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_bands_cause">Likely cause: row-wise refresh dropout — upload interrupted during a specific segment, or the module lost power mid-refresh.</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_bands_fix">Fix: Run horizontal bars test. Missing bands indicate which rows failed. Clear panel first if the image is unreadable.</string>

    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_noise_title">Random noise</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_noise_cause">Likely cause: severe transfer corruption (tag lost repeatedly) or the module controller is wedged after multiple interrupted refreshes.</string>
    <string name="troubleshoot_symptom_noise_fix">Fix: Leave the module away from NFC for 5 minutes (full discharge), then Clear panel (white). If noise persists on a solid white pattern, try another phone to rule out the module.</string>

